	'rooms_s0_h' => 'One floor, five rooms',
	'rooms_s0_p0' => 'The five rooms share a single floor of the old customs warehouse at 12 Quay Street, joined by corridors you can follow on the line plan. Meridian Hall, the Linden Room, the Atrium and Studio Rooms 1 to 4 can run as one congress floor: plenary in the hall, posters in the Atrium, breakouts in the studios. The Quay Room sits aside from that circuit as a boardroom of 16, with a window toward the harbour. You walk from a session to a break without changing buildings.',
	'rooms_s0_p1' => 'Capacities are the numbers we contract to. Meridian Hall is 420 in theatre or 260 at banquet. The Linden Room is 120 in classroom or 160 in theatre. The Atrium is 300 standing. Each Studio Room holds 24 to 36. A full day and a half day are both bookable. A half day is 60 percent of the full-day rate, and a free provisional hold lasts 48 hours while you confirm the combination.',
	'ia_room_meridian_webp' => 'Meridian Hall set theatre style, empty, with a low stage and brick walls.',
