	'meridian-hall_s1_p1' => 'The foyer desk is set for arrivals, with lanyards, from 7:30, after the coordinator has already been in the building for half an hour. Tomás Ferreira, head of events, turns the room list into the run sheet: which layout, which hours inside 7:00 to 23:00, which studios are live in which block. The plenary stays in Meridian. The hall is not broken into smaller rooms.',
	'meridian-hall_s2_h' => 'Pairs well with the Atrium and the Studios',
	'meridian-hall_s2_p0' => 'Meridian Hall pairs with the Atrium and with Studio Rooms 1 to 4. The Atrium holds 300 standing, so posters, a small exhibition or a reception can stay open while the hall turns around between sessions. The four studios hold 24 to 36 people each, which is enough for parallel breakouts without borrowing the Linden Room. Said as one line, Meridian Hall, the Atrium and the Studios are one congress floor.',
	'meridian-hall_s2_p1' => 'The Linden Room remains available on that floor when a stream needs classroom tables for 120 or theatre rows for 160, at €1,900 for a full day. The Quay Room, a boardroom for 16 at €640, can be held aside if officers need a closed table during the congress days. Name the extra rooms at enquiry. The free hold covers the rooms you list, for 48 hours, before any contract.',
