	'linden-room_lead' => 'The Linden Room holds 120 in classroom or 160 in theatre. It is the room for society workshops, training days and parallel sessions that do not need Meridian Hall.',
	'linden-room_s0_h' => 'Classroom, theatre and the day rate',
	'linden-room_s0_p0' => 'The Linden Room has two contracted layouts. Classroom seating is 120, at tables. Theatre seating is 160, in rows. It is the room for society workshops, training days and parallel sessions that should not be stretched across Meridian Hall. The full-day rate is €1,900. A half day is 60 percent of the full-day rate. Water is set on the classroom tables. Standard AV is available with the day delegate package at €68 a person, which also covers a share of the room, two coffee breaks and lunch.',
	'linden-room_s0_p1' => 'The room is not the 420-seat hall and it is not the 16-seat boardroom. If your list sits near 120 or near 160, say so on the enquiry and we will place a free 48-hour hold on Linden while you confirm the date. Site visits to walk the room are on weekdays, by appointment, between 9:00 and 18:00.',
	'ia_case_forum_webp' => 'Teachers having lunch at long tables in the Atrium.',
	'linden-room_s1_h' => 'The teachers\' spring forum',
	'linden-room_s1_p0' => 'The Halden Teachers\' Association used the Linden Room for its spring forum: 160 people, one day, with lunch in the Atrium. The headcount matched the theatre capacity, so the room was in rows rather than at classroom tables. Lunch moved into the Atrium, which holds 300 standing and took long tables for that midday break. The building was open from 7:00 to 23:00, as on any event day, and the coordinator was on site from 7:00.',
	'linden-room_s1_p1' => 'A one-day society meeting is the ordinary life of this room. People arrive, meet, eat, and leave. The run sheet, agreed with the contract, says which layout and when lunch is called. Lucía Romero\'s kitchen cooks to the delegate count. Priya Raman\'s registration list is where dietary notes are collected before the day, not at the table.',
	'linden-room_s2_h' => 'What sits beside it',
	'linden-room_s2_p0' => 'The Linden Room pairs with the Atrium when a workshop or a forum needs lunch, posters or a short reception and does not need Meridian Hall. That is the teachers\' pattern: Linden for the meeting, the Atrium for the meal. It can also run as a parallel stream beside a congress in Meridian, if one session needs classroom tables for up to 120 rather than a studio capped at 36.',
	'linden-room_s2_p1' => 'Studio Rooms 1 to 4 remain the smaller breakouts, at €420 each for a full day. If the day is a training day for a society, Linden alone is often the whole hire. If the list grows toward 260 at banquet or 420 in theatre, the booking belongs in Meridian Hall at €6,800 for a full day. Tell us the number at the first enquiry and we will name the room that fits it.',
