	'the-atrium_lead' => 'The Atrium holds 300 people standing. It is the room for poster sessions, exhibitions and receptions, on the same floor as the hall and the smaller meeting rooms.',
	'the-atrium_s0_h' => 'Standing room, for boards and tables',
	'the-atrium_s0_p0' => 'The Atrium is contracted at one capacity: 300 standing. It is a glazed room with brick walls, used for poster sessions, exhibitions and receptions, and for lunch when a forum wants long tables rather than a banquet hall. The full-day rate is €2,600. A half day is 60 percent of that rate. We do not publish a theatre or a classroom number here. Seated rows belong in Meridian Hall or the Linden Room.',
	'the-atrium_s0_p1' => 'Floor space for boards, an exhibition or a welcome gathering belongs here. Light comes from the glazing, which is why poster sessions are planned in this room and not in a corridor. If you need the Atrium only for the middle of the day, say so at the visit and we will look at the half-day rate before the contract is drawn. The free provisional hold is 48 hours, on this room or on a combination.',
	'ia_case_congress_webp' => 'A plenary session seen from the back of the hall with about four hundred delegates.',
	'the-atrium_s1_h' => 'Posters one day, lunch the next',
	'the-atrium_s1_p0' => 'Two gatherings show the room doing different work. At the Northern Society of Hospital Pharmacists\' annual congress, 420 delegates came for three days. Plenary sessions were in Meridian Hall, breakouts were in the four Studio Rooms, and the posters were in the Atrium. At the Halden Teachers\' Association spring forum, 160 people came for one day in the Linden Room, and lunch was served in the Atrium.',
	'the-atrium_s1_p1' => 'The same shell can hold boards through a congress morning and long tables at midday on a forum. Lucía Romero\'s kitchen sends the lunch and the coffee breaks. The day delegate package, at €68 a person, is the usual way those breaks and that lunch are covered, together with a share of the room and standard AV. The Atrium\'s own hire remains a separate line at €2,600 for a full day.',
	'the-atrium_s2_h' => 'How it joins the other rooms',
	'the-atrium_s2_p0' => 'On a congress floor the Atrium sits between Meridian Hall and Studio Rooms 1 to 4. Delegates leave a plenary, walk the posters, and go on to a breakout. The hall can reset while the boards stay open. On a smaller day the Atrium stands with the Linden Room alone, which is what the teachers did. It is rarely the right partner for a closed board meeting. That table is the Quay Room, for 16, at €640 for a full day.',
	'the-atrium_s2_p1' => 'Receptions stay inside event-day building hours, 7:00 to 23:00. Your coordinator is on site from 7:00, including when the Atrium is the first room guests see. At the site visit, tell us whether you need the space for posters, for lunch, for a reception, or for more than one of those, and the run sheet will record the order.',
