	'associations-congresses_lead' => 'An association congress here uses Meridian Hall, the Atrium and the Studio Rooms as one floor. The gathering we plan from is a three-day meeting of 420 delegates.',
	'associations-congresses_s0_h' => 'How 420 delegates use the building',
	'associations-congresses_s0_p0' => 'A congress at Kaigi Centre is planned across one floor. Meridian Hall seats 420 in theatre, and that is the plenary number we work to. The Atrium holds 300 standing, which is the place for poster sessions and a small exhibition. Studio Rooms 1 to 4 hold 24 to 36 each, so parallel groups leave the hall without leaving the building. The planning line is short: Meridian Hall, the Atrium and the Studios are one congress floor.',
	'associations-congresses_s0_p1' => 'The Linden Room, at 120 classroom or 160 theatre, can take an extra stream when the programme needs tables rather than another studio. The Quay Room can be added for a board of 16 if officers meet during the same days. On those days the building is open from 7:00 to 23:00. A half day in any one of the rooms is 60 percent of its full-day rate, if part of the programme is shorter than a day.',
	'associations-congresses_s1_h' => 'The hospital pharmacists\' congress',
	'associations-congresses_s1_p0' => 'The Northern Society of Hospital Pharmacists held its annual congress here. The figures are 420 delegates, three days, Meridian Hall for the plenary, the Atrium for posters, and four Studio Rooms for breakouts. That is the full set this kind of meeting asks for, and it is the congress we will walk you through on a site visit. We do not cite a stack of other years. Tomás Ferreira, head of events, turns the room list into a run sheet: which room, which layout, which block of the day.',
	'associations-congresses_s1_p1' => 'The path to that sheet is the same four steps as any booking. An enquiry places a free hold for 48 hours. A site visit follows on a weekday. The contract takes a 30 percent deposit and includes the run sheet. The balance is due 14 days after the event. Cancellation terms sit in that same contract.',
	'ia_foyer_arrival_webp' => 'The morning foyer with delegates arriving at the registration desk.',
	'associations-congresses_s2_h' => 'Poster sessions',
	'associations-congresses_s2_p0' => 'Poster sessions use the Atrium, not the aisles of Meridian Hall. Boards stand in the glazed room against the brick, and delegates move through at standing room up to 300. The hall can reset, or a speaker can take the stage, while the posters remain open next door. If the association also wants a reception, it is the same room, still on the Atrium\'s rate of €2,600 for a full day, not a second venue elsewhere on the harbour.',
	'associations-congresses_s2_p1' => 'A half day is 60 percent of that full day when the posters only need part of the hire. Say which at the visit, before the contract fixes the hours. Exhibition tables, if you have them, belong in this same standing layout. We will not place boards in a Studio that has been set for 24 to 36 people around a table.',
	'associations-congresses_s3_h' => 'Registration on a congress morning',
	'associations-congresses_s3_p0' => 'Priya Raman leads delegate services and registration. On a congress morning the foyer desk is set for arrivals, with lanyards, from 7:30. Your coordinator is already on site from 7:00, and the early facilities shift has been in the hall before that. The day delegate package, at €68 a person, is the usual way an association covers the delegate side of the day: a share of the room, two coffee breaks, lunch and standard AV.',
	'associations-congresses_s3_p1' => 'Dietary notes travel with the registration list to Lucía Romero\'s kitchen, so the lunch count matches the people who were invited, not a guess at the pass. The office that confirms those lists is open Monday to Friday, from 9:00 to 18:00. Amara Nwosu\'s setup crew turns the agreed layouts into chairs, tables and poster boards before the first delegate reaches Quay Street.',
