	'corporate-offsites_lead' => 'Leadership days use the Studio Rooms and the Quay Room. The offsite we plan from is two days for 36 people, in Studios 1 and 2 with the boardroom alongside.',
	'corporate-offsites_s0_h' => 'Studios for the group, the Quay Room for a smaller table',
	'corporate-offsites_s0_p0' => 'Leadership days and team days use Studio Rooms 1 to 4 and the Quay Room. Each studio holds 24 to 36 people, with a table and, if you want one, a blank flipchart. The full-day rate is €420 for each studio. The Quay Room is a boardroom for 16 at a long oak table, looking toward the harbour, at €640 for a full day. The pair is straightforward. The working group takes one or two studios.',
	'corporate-offsites_s0_p1' => 'The conversation that needs a closed table of up to 16 takes the Quay Room. A half day in either is 60 percent of the full-day rate. Meridian Hall, at 420 theatre seats, is the wrong room for a group of 36, and we will say so at enquiry. The Atrium can be added for a reception of up to 300 standing. Most team days never need it. The building on an event day is open from 7:00 to 23:00.',
	'ia_case_offsite_webp' => 'Eight colleagues discussing around a blank whiteboard in a Studio Room.',
	'corporate-offsites_s1_h' => 'Arden Logistics, two days, 36 people',
	'corporate-offsites_s1_p0' => 'Arden Logistics booked a leadership offsite for 36 people over two days, in Studio Rooms 1 and 2, plus the Quay Room. Thirty-six is the top of a single studio\'s range, so the second studio gave the group a place to split and a place to gather again. The Quay Room took the conversations that needed a board table rather than the full group. This is the offsite we describe. We do not keep a public list of other companies.',
	'corporate-offsites_s1_p1' => 'Tomás Ferreira\'s events team writes the two days onto one run sheet. Amara Nwosu\'s operations and setup crew set the studios to that sheet. Owen Mbeki\'s early facilities shift lays the tables before people arrive, the same early work you see in the empty hall on a congress morning. Your coordinator is on site from 7:00 on both days. The deposit is 30 percent on contract, and the balance is due 14 days after the event.',
	'corporate-offsites_s2_h' => 'How a team day is paced',
	'corporate-offsites_s2_p0' => 'A team day starts when the building opens at 7:00. The coordinator is here from that hour, and the studio is already set: table, chairs, and a blank flipchart if the run sheet asked for one. People arrive into a room that is finished, not into a room still being built. The morning is the working session in the studio. Lunch follows if you have taken the day delegate package, at €68 a person, which brings two coffee breaks and lunch as well as a share of the room and standard AV.',
	'corporate-offsites_s2_p1' => 'The afternoon can move to the Quay Room when a smaller group needs the table of 16, then return to the studio to close. A second day uses the same rooms, already named on the sheet. Hours sit inside the event-day window of 7:00 to 23:00 and are fixed at contract. Daniel Kowalski\'s AV team covers the standard technical set. Anything beyond that is written down before the day, not invented at the door.',
	'corp_cta' => 'Plan an event →',
