	'corporate-offsites_r3_l' => 'Day package',
	'corporate-offsites_r3_v' => '€68 a person',
	'plan-an-event_lead' => 'A booking moves in four steps: a free 48-hour hold, a weekday site visit, a contract with the run sheet and a 30 percent deposit, then the event day with your coordinator here from 7:00.',
	'plan-an-event_s0_h' => 'Enquiry and the 48-hour hold',
	'plan-an-event_s0_p0' => 'The first step is an enquiry. Write or telephone the office, Monday to Friday, from 9:00 to 18:00. Give the date, the rooms, and the number of people. We place a provisional hold for 48 hours, and we do not charge for it. The hold covers the rooms you named, not the whole warehouse. It is long enough to check a date with a board or an association committee. If the room choice changes inside those 48 hours, tell us and we will adjust the hold.',
	'plan-an-event_s0_p1' => 'When the time runs out and you have not asked for a visit or a contract, the date returns to the open list. There is no fee for letting it go. A congress near 420 delegates starts with Meridian Hall. A forum near 160 starts with the Linden Room. A group of 24 to 36 starts with a Studio. A board of 16 starts with the Quay Room.',
	'plan-an-event_s1_h' => 'Site visit, contract and deposit',
	'plan-an-event_s1_p0' => 'The second step is a site visit on a weekday, by appointment, inside office hours. You walk the rooms in the hold. Meridian Hall if you are near 420 theatre or 260 banquet. The Linden Room for 120 classroom or 160 theatre. The Atrium for 300 standing. A Studio for 24 to 36. The Quay Room for 16. The third step is the contract and the run sheet. The contract names the rooms, the days, the layouts and the rate.',
	'plan-an-event_s1_p1' => 'The deposit is 30 percent, due on contract. The balance is due 14 days after the event. A half day is billed at 60 percent of the full-day rate. Cancellation is free until 90 days before the event. Between 89 and 30 days the cancellation charge is 50 percent. Under 30 days it is 100 percent. The visit is the moment to decide, while the hold is still free and before those bands apply.',
	'ia_plan_sitevisit_webp' => 'A coordinator walking two visitors through an empty meeting room.',
	'plan-an-event_s2_h' => 'What does the run sheet contain?',
	'plan-an-event_s2_p0' => 'The run sheet is the working paper that travels with the contract. It names each room and the layout: theatre or banquet in Meridian Hall, classroom or theatre in the Linden Room, standing use in the Atrium, the studio numbers, and the Quay Room if you have it. It names the hours inside the event-day window of 7:00 to 23:00, including when registration opens. For a congress, that foyer desk, with Priya Raman\'s delegate services, is set from 7:30.',
	'plan-an-event_s2_p1' => 'It records the day delegate package where you have taken it, at €68 a person, so the kitchen and the AV desk share one headcount. It names your coordinator, who is on site from 7:00 on the event day. The sheet does not replace the contract. Deposit, balance and cancellation stay in the contract. If a time changes after signing, the sheet is updated in writing from the office, on a weekday, rather than by a message sent to the crew on the morning.',
	'plan-an-event_s3_h' => 'Sending an enquiry',
	'plan-an-event_s3_p0' => 'The enquiry form on this page is the place to begin if you are not already in correspondence. Leave the organisation, a contact name, the preferred dates, the headcount and the rooms you think you need. If you already know the shape of the day, say so in plain words: a congress near 420, an offsite near 36, or a one-day forum near 160. We answer during office hours, Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00.',
	'plan-an-event_s3_p1' => 'The form does not book the site visit by itself and it does not take payment. The visit is arranged in the reply. The deposit comes later, on contract. If you would rather see the halls before you write, the open day is Saturday 14 November 2026. Hall tours run from 10:00 to 15:00 and do not need a booking. The address is 12 Quay Street, Halden Harbour, six minutes on foot from Halden Central.',
