	'ia_food_coffee_webp' => 'A coffee break table with ceramic cups, pastries and hands reaching for a cup.',
	'food-hospitality_lead' => 'The kitchen is led by Lucía Romero. Coffee breaks, lunch and the day delegate package are set on the run sheet, with the rooms and the headcount, before the event day.',
	'food-hospitality_s0_h' => 'Lucía Romero\'s kitchen',
	'food-hospitality_s0_p0' => 'Lucía Romero is head chef. The kitchen cooks for the headcount on the contract: a congress lunch, a forum table, or a quieter offsite, according to the rooms you have hired. It is not a restaurant with a door on the quay. On a congress day the count can follow a plenary that seated 420 in Meridian Hall. On a forum day it can be the long tables in the Atrium, as it was for the Halden Teachers\' Association, 160 people, after their session in the Linden Room.',
	'food-hospitality_s0_p1' => 'On an offsite it can be lunch for 36, the Arden Logistics number, without any banquet layout in the hall. Service times are written on the run sheet and sit inside event-day building hours, 7:00 to 23:00. The crew does not invent a second sitting on the morning. If the programme changes, the sheet changes first, through the office, on a weekday.',
	'food-hospitality_s1_h' => 'Coffee breaks and lunch',
	'food-hospitality_s1_p0' => 'The day delegate package includes two coffee breaks and lunch. The coffee break is a set break, with cups and pastries, not an all-day café in the foyer. Lunch is served in the room the run sheet names. For the teachers\' spring forum, that room was the Atrium. For a congress, lunch can leave Meridian Hall so the plenary room can reset while people eat. For a studio day, lunch stays with the group of 24 to 36, or with the two studios Arden Logistics used.',
	'food-hospitality_s1_p1' => 'The minutes of service are agreed when the programme is known, and they are copied onto the run sheet with the room names. We do not publish a sample menu with prices of its own. The food price we publish is the package, at €68 a person. A reception in the Atrium is a room conversation as well as a kitchen one. The Atrium itself is €2,600 for a full day, or 60 percent of that for a half day.',
	'food-hospitality_s2_h' => 'Dietary requirements',
	'food-hospitality_s2_p0' => 'Dietary needs are collected with the delegate list. Priya Raman\'s delegate services take them at registration, and the kitchen receives them before the event day. The run sheet carries the count. We would rather have a clear list at contract, or as names firm up with Tomás Ferreira\'s events team, than a correction at the coffee table. The same habit covers a three-day congress of 420 and a one-day forum of 160.',
	'food-hospitality_s2_p1' => 'If a requirement changes close to the day, write to the office on a weekday, between 9:00 and 18:00, and Lucía Romero\'s kitchen will amend what the prep can still meet. We will tell you plainly when a late change can no longer be cooked. Delegates should not have to explain a diet for the first time while a break is being served. Put it on the list that Priya already holds.',
	'food-hospitality_s3_h' => 'The package at €68',
	'food-hospitality_s3_p0' => 'Per person, the day delegate package is €68. It covers a share of the room, two coffee breaks, lunch and standard AV. It is the same figure on the rates table and in every proposal. It does not include the room hire. Meridian Hall remains €6,800 for a full day, the Linden Room €1,900, the Atrium €2,600, each Studio Room €420, and the Quay Room €640. You add €68 for each person who is actually attending, at the headcount written into the contract.',
	'food-hospitality_s3_p1' => 'Half-day room hire is 60 percent of the full-day room rate. When you plan, say whether people are with you for the whole building day, from the 7:00 open toward the 23:00 close, or for a shorter programme. The package is how associations, and one-day meetings in the manner of the teachers\' forum, cover food and standard AV in a single line. Room-only hire is equally clear: say so, and the breaks will not be assumed.',
