	'ia_district_plan_svg' => 'Line plan of the quay district: the warehouse, Halden Central station and the Quay Street tram stop.',
	'getting-here_lead' => 'Kaigi Centre is at 12 Quay Street, Halden Harbour, a six-minute walk from Halden Central station. Tram line 2 stops at Quay Street, at the door end of the same walk.',
	'getting-here_s0_h' => 'Station, tram and the six-minute walk',
	'getting-here_s0_p0' => 'Kaigi Centre is at 12 Quay Street, Halden Harbour. Halden Central is the rail station. From the station the walk to the door is six minutes. Tram line 2 stops at Quay Street, the stop that takes this street\'s name. The building is the converted harbour customs warehouse, brick along the quay, with the entrance on Quay Street. A line drawing of the district marks the quay, the station and the tram stop as one short walk.',
	'getting-here_s0_p1' => 'For a site visit, the office will confirm the door when the appointment is made. On an event morning, registration is in the foyer, and the walk from the tram is the same six minutes. Allow that walk inside your own start time. The building opens at 7:00 on an event day, and congress registration at the foyer desk is set from 7:30. The office, for a weekday visit, is a different clock: Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00.',
	'getting-here_s1_h' => 'Parking on the quay',
	'getting-here_s1_p0' => 'The quay has 62 parking spaces for people driving to an event or to a site visit. Sixty-two is the full number we publish. A congress of 420 delegates will not fit into those spaces, so the practical arrival for Meridian Hall is Halden Central or tram line 2 to Quay Street. A studio offsite of 36, or a board of 16 in the Quay Room, can treat the car park as a real share of the arrival. Coaches and large production vehicles should be raised at the site visit so the run sheet can say where they stop.',
	'getting-here_s1_p1' => 'The house team uses the loading dock for chairs, which is the trolley of stacked seats you will see in photographs of the crew. It is a working dock on an event morning, not a second public entrance. If someone in your group needs to be met at the Quay Street door, ask for that when the visit is booked, and the coordinator will know before 7:00 on the day.',
	'getting-here_s2_h' => 'Hours and the open day',
	'getting-here_s2_p0' => 'The office is open Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00. Enquiries and site visits by appointment sit inside those hours. On event days the building is open from 7:00 to 23:00, which covers early registration and an evening reception in the Atrium if the contract includes one. Your coordinator is on site from 7:00 on the event day. The public open day is Saturday 14 November 2026. Hall tours run from 10:00 to 15:00, and you do not need to book.',
	'getting-here_s2_p1' => 'That Saturday is the date we publish for unbooked tours. Room rates do not apply to a tour. If a tour leads you to want a date, the next step is the ordinary one: a free hold for 48 hours, then a weekday site visit, then a contract with a 30 percent deposit. The balance of a contracted event is due 14 days after the event, which has nothing to do with the open-day tour.',
	'getting-here_s3_h' => 'Reading the district plan',
	'getting-here_s3_p0' => 'The district plan is a pen line on white, in the same spirit as the floor plan inside the building. It shows the quay, Halden Central, and the Quay Street stop on tram line 2, with the warehouse at 12 Quay Street. There is one address. You are six minutes from the station on foot. The tram stop is the local one. For a site visit, come during office hours, Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00, to the appointment you have made.',
	'getting-here_s3_p1' => 'For the open day, follow the hall tours between 10:00 and 15:00 on Saturday 14 November 2026. The loading dock is where the team moves chairs before a large set-up in Meridian Hall. Guests on an event day use the Quay Street entrance and the foyer, where Priya Raman\'s registration desk opens at 7:30 for a congress. Keep the six-minute walk in mind if your people are coming from a train that arrives close to that time.',
