	'ia_exterior_quay_webp' => 'The brick warehouse facade on the quay in morning light.',
	'about_lead' => 'Kaigi Centre opened in 2009 in a converted 1920s harbour customs warehouse at 12 Quay Street. Seven people run the house, and each one has a named job on an event day.',
	'about_s0_h' => 'A customs warehouse, opened in 2009',
	'about_s0_p0' => 'The building on 12 Quay Street was a harbour customs warehouse in the 1920s. In 2009 it opened as Kaigi Centre, a conference house for associations and for corporate offsites. Ingrid Halvorsen has been director since that opening year. The rooms were planned as a network on one floor, and they are still that network: Meridian Hall, the Linden Room, the Atrium, Studio Rooms 1 to 4, and the Quay Room. The brick front on the quay is still the front people walk toward from Halden Central.',
	'about_s0_p1' => 'What the house is known for, in the way we talk about the work, is the hour before the doors fill. At 6:45 the early shift is in the empty hall, laying notepads along the rows. The line we use for that picture is a plain one: ready before you arrive. Event days then run from 7:00 to 23:00, with a coordinator on site from 7:00.',
	'ia_team_dock_webp' => 'Five staff laughing beside a trolley of stacked chairs at the loading dock.',
	'about_s1_h' => 'The seven people who run the house',
	'about_s1_p0' => 'Ingrid Halvorsen is director, and has been since 2009. Tomás Ferreira is head of events. He takes the enquiry, the weekday site visit and the run sheet through to contract. Amara Nwosu leads operations and the setup crew, the people who turn a layout on the sheet into tables and chairs. Daniel Kowalski leads AV and technical, including the sound desk at the back of Meridian Hall. Lucía Romero is head chef, responsible for the coffee breaks and the lunch inside the day delegate package.',
	'about_s1_p1' => 'Priya Raman leads delegate services and registration. She is who you meet when the foyer desk opens at 7:30, with lanyards, on a congress morning. Owen Mbeki is facilities on the early shift. He is the person laying notepads and pencils along the rows in the empty hall. The crew photograph shows five of the team at the loading dock with a trolley of stacked chairs. The list of seven is the list that matters. Roles are these, and they do not rotate into other titles.',
	'about_s2_h' => 'The way the house states its terms',
	'about_s2_p0' => 'We name a capacity and a rate, and then we stop. Meridian Hall is 420 in theatre or 260 at banquet, at €6,800 for a full day. The Linden Room is 120 classroom or 160 theatre, at €1,900. The Atrium is 300 standing, at €2,600. Each Studio Room is 24 to 36, at €420. The Quay Room is 16, at €640. A half day is 60 percent of the full-day rate. The day delegate package is €68 a person. A hold is free for 48 hours. The deposit is 30 percent on contract, and the balance is due 14 days after the event.',
	'about_s2_p1' => 'Cancellation is free until 90 days before the event, 50 percent from 89 days to 30 days, and 100 percent under 30 days. The gatherings we will describe are three: the pharmacists\' congress, the Arden Logistics offsite, and the teachers\' spring forum. The office that explains any of this is open Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00.',
